  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi, how are you holding up?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.59,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_16"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "A bit tired today, but okay.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.56,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_17"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Physics word problems. I read them and freeze.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.3,
   "block": "studying.dlg20",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Common one. Try a routine. First, write down every number they give you, with its unit.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 1.15,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "studying.dlg20"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hey Ines, did the surgery ring about your blood test?",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "nq_social_009",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "other_name",
   "phrasing": "nq_social_009",
   "name_pos": "start",
   "addressee": "Ines"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "other",
   "text": "Not yet. They said by Friday.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.81,
   "block": "nq_social_009"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Okay, then what?",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.83,
   "block": "studying.dlg20",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Write down what they're actually asking for. Then look for the formula that connects what you know to what you want.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.81,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "studying.dlg20"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Sometimes there are like",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 1.85,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "studying.dlg20"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "two formulas you need, though.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 2.61,
   "block": "studying.dlg20",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then work out the missing piece with the first formula, and use it in the second. Draw a quick sketch too, it helps a lot.",
   "est_sec": 7.85,
   "gap_before": 1.06,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "studying.dlg20"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "A sketch for physics?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "studying.dlg20",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes. Even a box with arrows for forces makes the problem much less scary.",
